# What must never enter the build context. Two reasons appear below: some of
# this would be wrong inside the image, and some of it would only make the
# upload slow.

# --- wrong inside the image -------------------------------------------------

# Runtime data: the SQLite database, its -wal and -shm files, generated report
# PDFs, QA output. A development database carries the demo staff accounts,
# whose passwords are published in the README, and a synthetic year of invented
# orders. It must never be baked into a restaurant's image.
var/

# Local configuration, which can hold real settings or a password.
.env
.env.*

# Built on the host for Windows; the image installs Linux packages with
# `npm ci`, and a Windows node_modules would break the build.
node_modules/

# Built inside the build stage from the source that is copied in.
dist/

# --- only makes the upload slow ---------------------------------------------

# Tests and visual QA: not needed to build the client or to run the server.
test/

# Reference mocks for the design system (17 MB of PNGs); documentation only.
design-lab/

# Dev-container definition: for editing this project, not for running it.
.devcontainer/

# Git metadata and editor noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
*.log
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# The deployment files themselves. Docker reads them from outside the context.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
render.yaml
fly.toml
